From: Abzu <abzu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] gui: authorize privileged operations via doas(1)

Abzu overlay (see ../README.md): security pillar -- GNUstep authorization
must not shell out to sudo/askpass. Replace the hardcoded `sudo -S`
front-end with `doas -u root`, which honours /etc/doas.conf (shipped by
build/derivations/rootfs.nix under the Abzu policy) and fails closed.

Upstreaming: tracked per-patch in docs/ROADMAP.md.

---
diff --git a/Source/GSSystemRootAction.m b/Source/GSSystemRootAction.m
index 8ed882d..901c112 100644
--- a/Source/GSSystemRootAction.m
+++ b/Source/GSSystemRootAction.m
@@ -3,9 +3,11 @@
   NSTask	*task = [NSTask new];
   NSMutableData *out = [NSMutableData new];
 
-  /* Default front-end: sudo reading the password from the askpass pipe. */
-  [task setLaunchPath: @"/usr/bin/sudo"];
-  [task setArguments: ([NSMutableArray arrayWithObject: @"-S"])];
+  /* Abzu overlay: doas(1) is the only supported privilege front-end;
+   * /etc/doas.conf is the single source of truth for who may run what. */
+  [task setLaunchPath: @"/usr/bin/doas"];
+  [task setArguments: ([NSMutableArray arrayWithObjects:
+			@"-u", @"root", nil])];
   [(NSMutableArray *)[task arguments] addObjectsFromArray: argv];
   [task setStandardOutput: [NSPipe pipe]];
   return YES;
